From: buntOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: input: mediatek,pmic-keys: add the power key hold time

Describe holding the power key to power off through the kernel, for boards
whose PMIC long press only resets.
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/mediatek,pmic-keys.yaml | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/mediatek,pmic-keys.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/mediatek,pmic-keys.yaml
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/mediatek,pmic-keys.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/mediatek,pmic-keys.yaml
@@ -58,6 +58,12 @@ properties:
 
   power-off-time-sec: true
 
+  mediatek,power-key-hold-sec:
+    description:
+      Holding the power key this long powers off through the kernel. The key
+      then reports one press and release when let go, not when pressed.
+    minimum: 3
+
   mediatek,long-press-mode:
     description: |
       Key long-press force shutdown setting
